{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/7244-two-man-pack","id":7244,"title":"Two-man pack?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-10T02:02:26-08:00","id":7244,"title":"Two-man pack?","content":"So I've got two players that I'm thinking of maybe trying to introduce to Werewolf. The problem is of course that there seems to be a need for three werewolves to form a pack. Thus I'm turning to the forums to get some aid in case this can be solved. All ideas and suggestions are welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T05:19:26-08:00","id":7297,"title":"","content":"Just rule that you don't require 3? Why hamstring the players because of something that arbitrary? Simplest solution, and it's certainly not going to harm gameplay at all. It'll barely impact it either in any real way. If it's really that big of an issue, suggest the Mentor merit or Retainer to reflect a third member who does aid them on the side, but doesn't take up as much as the spotlight as a full fledged NPC .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T06:41:08-08:00","id":7311,"title":"","content":"Here's why you need 3 Uratha for a pack:<br /> <br /> One Uratha is a lone wolf; Two, are a <b>couple</b>; Three are a pack.<br /> <br /> Make the third member an NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T07:32:30-08:00","id":7332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/7244-two-man-pack?p=7311#post7311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's why you need 3 Uratha for a pack:<br /> <br /> One Uratha is a lone wolf; Two, are a <b>couple</b>; Three are a pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very helpful there m8","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T07:51:52-08:00","id":7338,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle that I run, we use 2 players and an NPC controlled by me to make it a 3rd. Basically, in order to avoid plot points where they just defer to my character for everything, I intentionally had my character give good and bad ideas. At first the players did everything my character said, boy do they regret that now. On the other hand, if you don't do something like that, what you have your character say will typically be seen as more important and the players will do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T11:28:27-08:00","id":7525,"title":"","content":"Adding a third NPC sounds like a good idea to solve this dilemma although its very true that it should be played carefully so that they don't take it like a voice-of-instant-win. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the idea and all the other suggestions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T15:02:00-08:00","id":7676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Talum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/7244-two-man-pack?p=7332#post7332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very helpful there m8</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify: The connotations of a pair of Uratha, in a normal setting, it's a breach of the Oath just waiting to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T15:57:49-08:00","id":7713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/7244-two-man-pack?p=7676#post7676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to clarify: The connotations of a pair of Uratha, in a normal setting, it's a breach of the Oath just waiting to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>WHAT?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> AHHAHAHAHAHAHA!! Are you implying that sex is inevitable? being part of a pack does not even mean they live toghether! what if they are not into each other? what if they feel like brothers(maybe they are who knows)? what if they are both heterosexual and of the same sex? do they bone regardless? i didnt know forsaken where so open in that matter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Going with the topic; A useful tip that i would give you for making so called GMPCs is this: don't make them at all protagonic, make them the kind of character that works best as a suporting cast. Don't make them combat characters, and if posible make them incompetent in the areas where the characters are competent, also dont make them super charismatic because youll end up talking to yourself, enjoy that characters suffering so you wont make him/her your pet. What i found is that the best kind of GMPC is a know it all, socially awkward, clumsy but totally lovable nerd, he can dump exposition about the things the characters don't know and is often a coward in combat, also bad luck makes the players love him more... its a nice set up for when you inevitably kill them in a horrible way, just the look in the players face is ... like chocolate to me<br /> <br /> Alternatively and this depends on the group, if you are introducing them to werewolf you can make another character be the abusive alpha, just make him a total dick, that way you can introduce them to the setting (&quot;you have the first change and this guy explains it while beating you up with a crowbar because tough love&quot;) and have the players eventually conront him on his bullshit or have him sacrifice himself for them to toy with their emotions &quot;but he was an asshole!&quot; &quot;yeah but deep down he love you all and died for your sins&quot;<br /> <br /> Alternatively artenatively make the most lovable mentor character and have him die two game in, great way to introduce a recurring villain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T16:13:10-08:00","id":7720,"title":"","content":"Connotation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T17:31:09-08:00","id":7755,"title":"","content":"Chroniclers Guide: All you ever wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"d